grgB6q3M.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-08-12\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Titanic\",\"overview\":\"On the night of April 14, 1912, the RMS Titanic, on her maiden voyage from Southampton to New York, collides with an iceberg in the middle of the North Atlantic and sinks within a few hours, drowning 1,500 of its 2,200 passengers.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-08-19\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Evel Knievel\",\"overview\":\"Why did Evel Knievel, a daredevil performer who was famous for spectacular, airborne, motorcycle stunts, crash during his famous Caesars Palace, Las Vegas stunt?\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-08-26\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Dale Earnhardt Sr.\",\"overview\":\"On 18 February 2001, Dale Ernhardt is killed in a racing accident on the Daytona 500 track, in Florida U.S.A. Investigators take on the challenge of determining why such a relatively small crash caused the death of a racing superstar.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mrCHa05DPknjhXfi1WKkPgsWw1F.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-09-09\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Harrison Ford\",\"overview\":\"Actor Harrison Ford left Santa Monica airport in his vintage WWII restored fighter plane on March 5, 2015; he radioed the tower just minutes later saying something was wrong and he needed to land somewhere immediately.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-09-16\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Sully\",\"overview\":\"On Jan. 15, 2009, three minutes after takeoff on a routine flight from La Guardia, N.Y. to Charlotte, N.C., US Airways Flight 1549 suddenly fell from the sky; without power, veteran pilot Capt. Sully Sullenberger landed the plane in the Hudson River.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-09-23\",\"runtime\":0}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2016-02-20\"}","status"